Detailed Results of 2021 Population Census
6
As compared to 2011, the base (younger generation) and the top (older generation) of the population 
pyramid for 2021 were notably broader due to increases in newborns and the elderly population as well as a 
longer lifespan over the past ten years. Besides, the population size of most of the remaining age groups 
showed increase. 
Population aged 25-39 (189,631) was the largest, as non-resident workers, incoming migrants and local 
baby boomers born between 1980’s and early 1990’s were concentrated in this age group; this population 
accounted for 27.8% of the total population. On the other hand, the bars for the populations aged 15-24 and 
45-54 were narrower than other age groups, which was ascribable to the relatively low number of births in 
the late 1990’s and in 1970’s. 
