7
As regards the local population, those in the age groups of 5-9, 25-39 and 55-64 together accounted for 
46.6% of the local population. Those aged 55-64 (90,138) comprised 15.9%, indicating that population ageing 
is expected to accelerate as this group will become part of the elderly population in the coming decade.  
Meanwhile, women aged 15-49 (childbearing age) totalled 139,040, a decrease of 5,472 from 144,512 
in 2011. They represented 46.1% of the local female population, a drop of 11.3 percentage points from ten 
years ago; the decrease in the proportion of women of childbearing age would in turn affect the fertility rate. 
Analysed by age, population in the younger age group of 15-34 took up 52.8% of the total, down by 1.7 
percentage points from a decade ago; meanwhile, those in the older age group of 35-49 constituted 47.2%. 
Chart 5: Population Pyramid for Local Population, 2011 and 2021
The median age of the total population went up from 33.3 in 2001 and 37.0 in 2011 to 38.4 in 2021, 
reflecting the continuation of the ageing trend. When excluding non-resident workers and non-local students 
living in Macao, the median age of the local population increased from 38.1 in 2011 to 39.7. 
